A||N||2||fastback87||where can I find a GETRAG???||||5||
Z||000000||fastback87||12-07-2001||11:11 PM||||If I wanted a getrag for my new 86 4 speed what can be a donor car???  Or does it have to come out of a fiero?||||reg||5
Z||000001||jelly2m8||12-07-2001||11:53 PM||||Check with Rodney dickman, he has a list of which FWD getrags are compatable with the Fiero. He also sells different linkages to make them work in a Fiero.<P> You'll still need to round up the cable brackets and the slave bracket, and tranny mount brackets and cables. Maybe Rodney makes those too, i'm not sure on them.<P> You will also need a 5 spd shifter, the isuzu shifters are the same as the getrag ones.<P> For anyone that wants to know, I took a P22, and the Cavalier equivelant.  the internals between the 88-92 J-body getrags and Fiero internals (gear sets, shift forks, etc) are identical part numbers<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://users.eastlink.ca/~acook1/pegged%2001.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by jelly2m8 (edited 12-07-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||wcapman||12-08-2001||06:18 PM||||I just finished building a FWD 282 for a Fiero.  Got the tranny for $275.  Paid 225 for a competent shop to open it up and check it out completely.  I also had a Gleason Torsen limited slip put in.  I might have forgone the case opening if it hadn't been for that.  I just bought the FWD&gt;RWD brackets from Rodney for another 140, plus I got the axle reinforcement bearings for another 80.  Now since I have digital instruments the speedo will work out, but you will need to do something about it if you have stock instruments.<P>If all that is too much, contact Ed Parks for a replacement Getrag.  They go for around $1000. ||||reg||1
